# AI Exam Coach — Cursor rules

Read CLAUDE.md in repo root FIRST. It is the canonical agent context —
stack, phases, architecture patterns, standing rules. This file is a
Cursor-specific supplement.

## Absolute rules

- Hlib approves every merge. Never merge or push --force without an
  explicit "мержи" / equivalent.
- No DDL to production Supabase from code. SQL goes in supabase/NN_*.sql
  as a migration file for Hlib to run manually. Client code degrades
  gracefully until he does (PGRST205 for tables, PGRST202 for RPCs).
- Never touch, echo, or commit API keys or secrets. If one appears in
  chat, it must be rotated.
- CAVEMAN MODE for chat replies. Terse Russian when Hlib writes
  Russian/Ukrainian. Drop articles, filler, hedging. Code, commits,
  security responses stay normal English.
- Grill Hlib. For any non-obvious design decision, ask before coding.
- Never add a new AI vendor (OpenAI, Google, etc.) without an explicit
  yes — Decision Log #39.
- Never mock the database in tests. Fake the client surface (see
  src/lib/question-novelty.test.ts pattern).

## Repo shape (skim)

- api/                     Vercel serverless (AI proxy, cron, unsubscribe)
- src/bootstrap.ts         Ordered legacy-module load — DO NOT REORDER
- src/main.tsx             React entry
- src/features/chat/AIChat.jsx    The big one: Coach modes, Practice, Speed Round, Exam Sim, Learn theory + flashcards
- src/features/learn/      Phase 3.7 skill-tree section
- src/stores/*.jsx         Legacy stores, publish window.* getters/setters
- src/lib/*.ts             New TypeScript modules (data-sync, math-render, speech, svg-sanitize, ...)
- src/i18n/i18n.jsx        5 languages: en / uk / ru / fr / de
- supabase/*.sql           Ordered migrations
- docs/phase-*-plan.md     Plan docs — read the current phase's before touching related code

## Architecture patterns

- Legacy stores publish getFoo / saveFoo / subscribeFoo / migrateFoo on
  `window`. Migration functions normalise data, never throw.
- New TS modules reach the legacy layer via `window.*` calls. Bootstrap
  order in src/bootstrap.ts is the only serialization guarantee.
- Sync: `src/lib/data-sync.ts` patches localStorage.setItem once at
  init; PERSONAL_DATA_KEYS in `src/stores/auth-store.jsx` is the
  allowlist for what pushes to Supabase.
- AI calls: always `window.brainComplete`, never `window.claude.complete`
  directly. brainComplete injects buildLearnerContext() + language hint.
- Structured AI JSON: use `window.parseJSON` OR
  `raw.slice(raw.indexOf("{"), raw.lastIndexOf("}") + 1)`. Set a race
  timeout of 30-45s.
- Any new module publishing a window global must add its name to
  REQUIRED_GLOBALS in src/bootstrap.ts.

## Coding style

- Explain WHY, not WHAT. Every file opens with a header on why it
  exists. Inline comments only for non-obvious constraints, workarounds,
  or surprising behavior.
- Don't add features, refactoring, or abstractions beyond what the task
  requires. A bug fix doesn't need surrounding cleanup.
- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones. New file needs
  a real reason.
- Never invent English abbreviations (cfg, impl, req). They tokenize the
  same as the full word.
- Test files sit next to their target: foo.ts → foo.test.ts.
- Migrating jsx → tsx: keep the exact window-global contract, just add
  types. Don't restructure at the same time.

## Workflows

### New phase / feature

1. Branch: phase-3.7X/short-slug
2. If non-trivial: write docs/phase-3-7X-plan.md (MVP scope, deferred,
   Decision Log, reversibility, "what could break silently" table)
3. SQL migration if needed (supabase/NN_*.sql WITH verification block)
4. Tests alongside code
5. Gate: `npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npx vitest run && npm run build`
6. Commit body explains WHY
7. Push, open PR, wait for "мержи"

### External services (all optional in dev)

- Supabase: cyftpdiabopydwytyudt project. Client anon key already
  hardcoded in auth-store.jsx (safe — RLS enforces isolation).
- Vercel: Hobby plan. Cron `0 16 * * *`.
- Resend: sandbox sender by default, no domain yet.
- OneSignal: Web Push only; site config in dashboard must be saved,
  OneSignalSDKWorker.js served from /public.
- Claude: server proxy at /api/complete. Never call the API directly
  from the client.

## Anti-patterns to reject

- Silent try/catch that swallows everything without a comment saying WHY
- Adding a comment that just restates the next line of code
- Introducing a new dependency for one utility function (write the
  utility)
- Renaming a public window global — every consumer breaks silently
  because REQUIRED_GLOBALS won't catch removal of one already-required
  name
- Bumping a package major version as a side effect of another change
- Adding a new AI vendor to solve a single feature (see Decision Log
  #39)
- "Just re-run the migration" — always additive, never destructive

## Language

Match Hlib's language in the current message. Ru/Uk → respond
caveman-terse Russian. En → respond English (caveman-terse still). Code,
commit messages, PR bodies stay full English.
